        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=x^2-8x+3\\\\y&=-2x-6\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3,-12)$",
          "worked": "Substitute $y=-2x-6$ into $y=x^2-8x+3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-2x-6&=x^2-8x+3\\\\x^2-6x+9&=0\\\\(x-3)^2&=0\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $x=3$ into $y=-2x-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-2(3)-6\\\\y&=-12\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is $(3,-12)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-76d80-p20-practice-slot-9-slot-9-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=9x^2+4\\\\y&=12x\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\frac23,8\\right)$",
          "worked": "Substitute $y=12x$ into $y=9x^2+4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}12x&=9x^2+4\\\\9x^2-12x+4&=0\\\\(3x-2)^2&=0\\\\3x-2&=0\\\\x&=\\frac{2}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{2}{3}$ into $y=12x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=12\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\\\y&=8\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is $\\left(\\frac{2}{3},8\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
